instruction:
In the sandbox model (Contoso, EXTENSION_PREFIX=Con), add a Chain-of-Command wrapper for SalesFormLetter_Invoice.promptAndRun(). The whole point of this case is that SalesFormLetter_Invoice does NOT declare promptAndRun — it only INHERITS it — so a member listing of that one class does not show the method at all. "Not in the list" means "not declared here", never "does not exist": walk the extends chain through the grounded path (get_object_info(objectType="class") / get_method / find_object against the symbol index; extension_info(mode="points") on SalesFormLetter_Invoice must also list promptAndRun as a CoC-eligible wrap point) until you reach the class that actually DECLARES it. Ground the pattern with get_knowledge(topic="class-inheritance"). Produce exactly ONE artifact through the grounded create path: a final extension class named SalesFormLetter_InvoiceCon_Extension carrying [ExtensionOf(classStr(SalesFormLetter_Invoice))] (pass objectName "SalesFormLetter_Invoice_Extension" and let the writer inject the Con infix; `create` prefixes only objectName, never names embedded in sourceCode, so the class name in the declaration and the classStr(...) argument must be spelled out by you exactly as they must end up). The [ExtensionOf] MUST name the SUBCLASS SalesFormLetter_Invoice (the narrow scope) even though the method is declared on a base class — do NOT retarget the wrapper at the declaring class, do NOT overlayer, do NOT subclass anything. The wrapper method must be exactly this text, with no additional behaviour in the body:

/// <summary>
/// Chain of Command wrapper for a method the augmented class only inherits.
/// </summary>
public void promptAndRun()
{
    // Declared on: <DeclaringClass>
    // Chain: <Chain>
    next promptAndRun();
}

where <DeclaringClass> is the name of the class that actually declares promptAndRun, and <Chain> is the full extends chain written as class names joined by ' -> ', starting at SalesFormLetter_Invoice and ending at the last X++ class before Object (do not write Object itself). Both values must be resolved from the symbol index — they are the observable proof that the declaring class was discovered rather than guessed, and the golden pins them. The two facts MUST be written as `//` line comments INSIDE the method body, exactly as shown, and MUST NOT be moved into the `///` XmlDoc header (e.g. a <remarks> block): the golden normalizer collapses every contiguous run of `///` lines to a single `/// <xmldoc/>` placeholder, so a declaring class recorded there is erased before the diff and the golden would score identically for a completely wrong answer. Keep the `///` <summary> header — its PRESENCE is what BPXmlDocNoDocumentationComments measures — but keep the pinned facts out of it. PREREQUISITE: the sandbox model's Descriptor must list ApplicationSuite in ModuleReferences (SalesFormLetter and SalesFormLetter_Invoice live in ApplicationSuite\Foundation) or the build fails with "does not specify a known class" even though the symbol index resolves the names fine. The class must build clean, and a clean build alone is not accepted as proof — read the written AxClass XML back and verify the declaration, the [ExtensionOf] target, the method name and the two doc-comment lines before finishing. There is deliberately NO SysTest for this case: runtime firing of a subclass wrapper is out of scope because SysTestConsole.exe / SysTestRunner.exe do not exist on the eval VM, so the oracle is the golden AxClass XML plus the clean build.
